WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.530
A crime scene.

2
00:00:01.580 --> 00:00:04.840
A trace of DNA, too small to see.

3
00:00:04.890 --> 00:00:08.720
Almost all of that DNA
is shared by every human.

4
00:00:08.770 --> 00:00:12.660
Yet DNA can link a sample
from a scene to one person.

5
00:00:12.710 --> 00:00:14.980
Identical twins are the exception.

6
00:00:15.030 --> 00:00:20.510
So if almost all human DNA is shared,
how can a trace of it point to just one

7
00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:21.680
person?

8
00:00:21.730 --> 00:00:25.600
In this mission, you'll make
a DNA profile in four steps:

9
00:00:25.650 --> 00:00:29.500
extract, amplify, separate, detect.

10
00:00:29.550 --> 00:00:32.730
Then you'll read DNA
profiles, lane by lane,

11
00:00:32.780 --> 00:00:34.910
as a forensic scientist would.

12
00:00:34.960 --> 00:00:39.970
Your mission: explain how a trace
of DNA can point to just one person.
